{"url": "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/fin-aid-scholarships/index.html", "final_url": "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/fin-aid-scholarships/index.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Financial Aid & Scholarships: Admissions: School of Science: Indiana University Indianapolis\nSkip to Content\nSkip to Main Navigation\nSkip to Search\nSchool of\nScienceIndianapolis\nDepartments\nBiology\nChemistry & Chemical Biology\nComputer Science\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nForensic & Investigative Sciences\nMathematical Sciences\nNeuroscience\nPhysics\nPsychology\nDepartments\nBiology\nChemistry & Chemical Biology\nComputer Science\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nForensic & Investigative Sciences\nMathematical Sciences\nNeuroscience\nPhysics\nPsychology\nToggle Search Box\nSearch\nSearch\nSchool of ScienceToggle Menu\nAboutAbout\nDean's Welcome\nVision, Mission & Values\nDean's Advisory Council\nFacts & Statistics\nNews\nEvents\nIU Indianapolis\nCommunity Outreach\nEmployment Opportunities\nContact\nAdmissionsAdmissions\nApply\nVisit\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nAdmitted Students\nAcademicsAcademics\nAreas of Study\nDegrees & Programs\nHonors Program\nCourses\nStudy Abroad\nAcademic Support\nDean's List and Science Scholars\nGraduation\nPoster Printing\nResearchResearch\nCenters & Partners\nStudent Opportunities\nStudent LifeStudent Life\nLive & Learn Downtown\nStudent Organizations\nHousing\nCareer ServicesCareer Services\nAdvising\nCareer Tools\nHandshake\nGraduate & Professional School Planning\nFor Employers\nFaculty & Staff\nInternship Scholarship\nElective Courses\nCareer Fairs\nHealth Professions Fair\nEvents\nContact Us\nAlumni & GivingAlumni & Giving\nGive to Science\nGet Involved\nEvents\nContact Us\nPeople Directory\nHome\nAdmissions\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nGet help paying for your science education\nWe know that an education here is a big investment. But as a student in the School of Science, you can feel confident that it will pay dividends after graduation and that you\u2019ll walk away with in-demand skills and the experience you need to succeed right out of the gate.\nReasonable tuition and fees, ample scholarship opportunities, and financial aid programs make the IU Indianapolis School of Science a smart choice. And, of course, there are ways to make your education more affordable. More than 85% of IU Indianapolis undergraduates receive financial aid.\n51%School of Science students received aid\n$1 millionin scholarships and financial aid awarded by the School of Science each year\nReduced tuition for out-of-state students\nStudents living outside of Indiana can get a reduced tuition that is closer to our current in-state student rate.\nIf you live in Kansas, Minnesota, Missouri, Nebraska, North Dakota, Ohio, or Wisconsin, you might be eligible for the Midwest Student Exchange Program (MSEP) Award.\nIf you\u2019re eligible, you\u2019ll save 57% on the normal out-of-state tuition.\nUndergraduate Illinois, Kentucky, Michigan, and Puerto Rico residents who qualify for the Indiana Partners tuition also receive a 57% reduction in normal out-of-state tuition.\nLearn more about reduced tuition\nFind the right financial aid and scholarship opportunities for you\nFind financial support for undergraduates\nFind financial support for graduate students\nLearn about funding for international students\nExplore School of Science scholarships\nNeed to talk to someone about financial aid?\nIf you have questions or just need help navigating the process, you can reach out to the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships at iuindy.finaid@iu.edu.\nFor questions about graduate financial aid, please email iuindy.gradaid@iu.edu.\nApply\nVisit\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nScholarships\nAdmitted Students\nSchool of Science\n402 N. Blackford Street\nIndianapolis, IN 46202\nEmail us\nSchool of Science\nDegrees and Majors\nResearch\nCareer Services\nAlumni and Giving\nApply\nVisit\nSearch our People Directory\nInformation for Faculty and Staff\nDepartments & Programs\nBiology\nChemistry & Chemical Biology\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nForensic & Investigative Sciences\nMathematical Sciences\nNeuroscience\nPhysics\nPsychology\nConnect with us\nSupport us\nIU Trident\nAccessibility\nCollege Scorecard\nOpen to All\nPrivacy\nNotice\nCopyright\n\u00a9 2026 The Trustees of\nIndiana\nUniversity", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/fin-aid-scholarships/index.html#content"], ["Skip to Main Navigation", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/fin-aid-scholarships/index.html#local-nav"], ["Skip to Search", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/fin-aid-scholarships/index.html#_search"], ["School of Science Indianapolis", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/"], ["Biology", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/biology/index.html"], ["Chemistry & Chemical Biology", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/chemistry/index.html"], ["Computer Science", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/cs/index.html"], ["Earth and Environmental Sciences", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/earthsciences/index.html"], ["Forensic & Investigative Sciences", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/forensic/index.html"], ["Mathematical Sciences", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/math/index.html"], ["Neuroscience", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/neuroscience/index.html"], ["Physics", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/physics/index.html"], ["Psychology", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/psychology/index.html"], ["Biology", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/biology/index.html"], ["Chemistry & Chemical Biology", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/chemistry/index.html"], ["Computer Science", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/cs/index.html"], ["Earth and Environmental Sciences", "https://science.indianapolis.iu.edu/earthsciences/index.html"], ["Forensic &